---
code: K0036
title: Bad Assert
severity: ERROR
since: 0.1.0
category: parse
deprecated: False
tags: [parse, syntax, assert, test, unit-testing]
description: "'assert' statement arguments are missing or malformed"
---

An `assert` statement inside a `test` block must follow the form `assert(condition)` or `assert(condition, "message")`. The optional second argument must be a string literal (plain or interpolated), and no trailing comma is permitted after the message.

## Example

This error occurs when `assert` is missing its condition, passes a non-string failure message, or includes a trailing comma after the message string:

```kura
test "math" {
  assert()
  assert(2 + 2 == 4, 123)
  assert(2 + 2 == 4, "math broke",)
}
```

## Solution

Pass a boolean condition expression and, optionally, a string failure message without a trailing comma:

```kura
test "math" {
  assert(2 + 2 == 4)
  assert(2 + 2 == 4, "expected 2 + 2 to equal 4")
}
```
